<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardo de Monteagudo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1789">1789</a>–<a href="/years/1825">1825</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Monteagudo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernardo de Monteagudo was a revolutionary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-wars-of-independence">Spanish American wars of independence</a>, born in Tucumán. He served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> in Chile and then in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, where as minister of war and foreign affairs in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> he dominated government. His harsh measures against Spaniards made him hated, and he was deposed and exiled in 1822. He was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1825.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-monteagudo.jpg" alt="Bernardo de Monteagudo" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: V.S. Noroña · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernardo_de_Monteagudo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
